  "result": "`npm test` now passes: 243 of 243 tests, up from 2 failures. There were two bugs in `src/`, and I didn't touch the tests.\n\n1. **`src/cart.js`: tax was charged before the discount.** The code comment says the discount comes off the pre-tax subtotal and tax applies to what's left, but the code ran them the other way round. I swapped the order, so a $100 cart with a $20 fixed discount and 10% tax now comes to (100 − 20) × 1.1 = 88 instead of 90.\n2. **`src/discount.js`: a fixed discount could push the total below zero.** A $20 discount on a $5 item gave −14.50. It's now capped at zero with `Math.max(0, …)`, which matches the code comment that a discount \"can bring the subtotal down to zero but never below.\"\n\nPercent discounts gave the same result before and after the reorder, which is why only the two fixed-discount tests were failing.",
